You could consider conditionally using `io.Reader` when using Python 3.14+. It is nearly identically defined, with one difference (pos-only length argument) that I would suggest adding:

```suggestion
@runtime_checkable
class SupportsRead(Protocol[_T_co]):
    def read(self, length: int = ..., /) -> _T_co: ...
```

So I like that this as a simpler option to the two hasattr checks, but we'd still have to leave those in place for StringIO-like objects, so it would end up being a somewhat redundant portion of the conditional.

I do, however, think we're likely going to want to extract [this logic](https://github.com/nateprewitt/requests/blob/f5c59743e7a45b68eaa82c83baaaed5607348afe/requests/utils.py#L78-L98) into it's own function in order to solve #3079 so maybe it could fit in with that somehow? I haven't worked up a good solution for that yet though.

