```

I am making this suggestion to solve two things I see as issues (you can argue that these are niche edge cases, but I think that the changes I suggest are reasonable) with the current implementation:

 1. As indicated in [RFC 2045](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2045#section-5.1), matching of attributes (of which `boundary` is one) is always case insensitive (thus `BOUNDARY="abcd"` would also work) - so I have added a call to `lower()` on line 32;
 2. The implementation with `split` will fail on a boundary that contains the `boundary=` substring. I think the intent is clearer if we write code that simply removes the prefix, and also reduces the number of potential edge cases;

